<svg class="dg" viewBox="0 0 1100 712" role="img" aria-labelledby="dg-title dg-desc">
<title id="dg-title">How Sub-Sub works</title>
<desc id="dg-desc">You use Sub-Sub in the browser view or in the terminal. Sub-Sub runs in pi on your computer and sends your messages to the model provider that you choose. It reads the library through the zotero server and uses the scholar server and, if it is on, the verify server (Starbuck). A switch, Library changes, decides whether it may also change the library through the zotero server. The profile removes some tools. Every library change goes through the approval gate. The zotero server talks to Zotero on 127.0.0.1 and keeps a journal of changes for undo. The servers use online services such as PubMed, Europe PMC, OpenAlex, Crossref, Unpaywall and Open Library. Sub-Sub writes everything in one Sub-Sub folder, which can sit inside an Obsidian vault, and reads its settings from your configuration folder.</desc>
